The page body is now stored in the `main` region of `blocks`, with `"@type": "plate"`, instead of the `__somersault__` block. Content with the old block is renamed when it is read, through the new `contentMigration` utility type, and keeps the new shape once it is saved. The backend must run Plone 6.2 with `plone.restapi` 10.3.0 or later before deploying this version, so that `plate` regions are indexed, checked for link integrity, and get `resolveuid` links. See the upgrade guide. @sneridagh
